A||||9||bocefas||Headlights for winter||||5||
Z||000000||bocefas||11-26-2001||12:09 PM||||Ok, I was just wondering if it would be a smart idea to put my headlights up and leave them up for the winter?  I have the later style headlight motors, which I understand are designed to "stall" and shut off without damage, but I thought I'd put out the topic and get everyone's 2 cents worth.  Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Tigger||11-26-2001||12:20 PM||||Yes you can leave them up.  Open the hood, turn on the lights then disconnect the plug on the single blue wire.<P>Another method, probably better is to upplug the blue wire, then manually crank the headlight up using the knob.  Be careful when you connect the wire again... the headlight will go up or down depending on the switch.  You just don't want to have your hand or fingers in the way if it jumps.<P>Wrap the plug ends with tape and carefully close the hood.  I think a few people here on the forum leave them up for the winter.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 11-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||11-26-2001||12:28 PM||||Tigger's correct except for the "single blue wire" part.  For later-style headlight system  , unplug the (only) connector going to the headlight motor on each side.  Or, wire-in a "leave up" switch on the dash like I have.<P>BTW, Tigger's "single blue wire" method is correct, for the older-style, relay-controlled (1984-1986) headlights  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||11-26-2001||12:49 PM||||Hehe, was going on what my '84 has.  Didn't realize they were different, now I know.<P>Thanks||||reg||3
Z||000004||FieroBUZZ||11-26-2001||02:26 PM||||NOW you tell me to watch my fingers  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>Darn thing near dragged me into the front compartment.<BR>Gary||||reg||9
Z||000005||bocefas||11-26-2001||03:30 PM||||Oh I know HOW to do it, I just didn't knopw if there was a good reason to or not.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tigger||11-26-2001||03:52 PM||||Yes, good idea, especially if your Fiero is going to sit outside and not going to be used everyday.  Then again if you clear the snow off before it builds and freezes up, you should be ok.<P>Sorry, didn't mean to sound insulting, just posted a FYI for anyone that happens to look at this post and are curious on how to do it.  I have a bad habit of doing that.  Actually, that's why I edited the post and explained how to do it.  Should have left it as "I think a few people here on the forum leave them up for the winter." <P>I mean a lot of people here will admit they had trouble finding the gas door lever the first time.        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Been covered before BTW...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001645.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001645.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20010706-2-006490.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20010706-2-006490.html</A> <p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 11-26-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000007||NEO Cesek Racing||11-26-2001||05:20 PM||||i'll own up to that one. i looked for 5 minutes before calling the guy i bought it from and asking how the hell you put gas in it. <BR>as for this headlight thing, why should i leave them up? so they don't freeze shut and i fry the motors? never heard anything about this.||||reg||1
Z||000008||NEO Cesek Racing||11-26-2001||05:26 PM||||nevermind, answered my own question. i gotta learn to read everything on here before i post. <BR>later||||reg||1
Z||000009||theogre||11-26-2001||07:08 PM||||I leave mine up if it's crappy and likely to freeze. better to leave them up then risk it. other wise I just run them normal.<P>you can always add the switch in the "down" wire, then you don't have to mess with the connectors and risk breaking the latches off. To do that you just stick a switch in the white wire comming off the headlight switch. Turn off the switch and the lights stay up.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
